        <headline>Gale Warning issued September 25 at 6:37AM EDT until September 26 at 7:00AM EDT by NWS Wakefield VA</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Northeast winds 20 to 30 kt with gusts up to 40 kt and
waves 4 to 6 ft.

* WHERE...Chesapeake Bay from Smith Point to Windmill Point VA
and Chesapeake Bay from Windmill Point to New Point Comfort VA.

* WHEN...Until 7 AM EDT Saturday.

* IMPACTS...Strong winds will cause hazardous waves which could
capsize or damage vessels and reduce visibility.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Northeast winds could briefly diminish to
20 to 25 kt with gusts to 30 kt this afternoon, but will
increase again this evening into early Saturday morning.
</description>
        <instruction>Mariners should alter plans to avoid these hazardous conditions.
Remain in port, seek safe harbor, alter course, and/or secure the
vessel for hazardous conditions.</instruction>
